Subject: arm64: dts: exynos7870-on7xelte: run the eMMC at HS200

The eMMC on the SM-G610F (Samsung AJNB3R, EXT_CSD rev 7, DEVICE_TYPE
0x57: HS52, DDR52, HS200 and HS400 at 1.8 V) is left at 25 MHz legacy
timing because mmc0 has no speed capabilities. Allow high speed and
HS200 (1.8 V); dw_mmc-exynos tunes the sample phase.

Measured on the phone (7.3.4, one-shot boots): sequential read 21.6 ->
137.9 MB/s, 4k random read 3365 -> 6026 IOPS, direct write 17.9 -> 53.7
MB/s; 256 MiB write + sha256 verify matches; 15 min fio random
read/write with crc32c verify: 26 GiB read, 25 GiB written, no error,
no mmc0/ext4 message. (cap-mmc-highspeed alone gives DDR52: 74.5 MB/s.)
HS400 is not enabled (no vendor hs400 timing data).

Against: linux v7.3.4 + 0001-0017. License: GPL-2.0 (kernel DTS).

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7870-on7xelte.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7870-on7xelte.dts
@@ -862,6 +862,12 @@
 	samsung,dw-mshc-sdr-timing = <0 4>;
 	samsung,dw-mshc-ddr-timing = <2 4>;
 	non-removable;
+	/*
+	 * The AJNB3R eMMC (EXT_CSD DEVICE_TYPE 0x57) supports HS200 at 1.8 V;
+	 * without these the card stays at 25 MHz legacy timing.
+	 */
+	cap-mmc-highspeed;
+	mmc-hs200-1_8v;
 
 	status = "okay";
 };
